NC Medicaid does **not** cover certain ambulance services even when an ambulance was dispatched. Under current **Policy 15, Ambulance Services** (effective **Dec. 15, 2023**), the main non-covered categories are:

## General non-covered situations
Ambulance services are not covered if:

- the beneficiary does **not** meet the eligibility requirements in Section 2.0;
- the beneficiary does **not** meet the coverage criteria in Section 3.0;
- the service **duplicates** another provider’s service; or
- the service is **experimental, investigational, or part of a clinical trial**.  
  [Ambulance Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/15-ambulance-services/download?attachment), § 4.1 (effective Dec. 15, 2023; current per amendment check)

## Ambulance-specific non-covered services
Policy 15 also specifically says NC Medicaid does **not** cover:

- **Loaded mileage** to a facility that is **not the nearest appropriate facility**;
- transport based on a **beneficiary’s preference** for a different facility;
- transport based on whether a physician **has staff privileges** at a hospital, because that does not determine whether the hospital is the appropriate facility;
- when **an ambulance is called and no treatment is needed**;
- **false alarm** ambulance responses;
- when the beneficiary **refuses all medical services**;
- ambulance transport for a medical service that is **not itself a Medicaid-covered service**;
- **commercial airline tickets**;
- **airstrip fees**;
- **taxes** charged separately;
- separate charges for **nursing personnel** who are employees of a facility or ambulance service;
- **waiting fees**; and
- separate charges for **oxygen, items, and supplies**, because those are included in the base rate and are not separately reimbursable.  
  [Ambulance Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/15-ambulance-services/download?attachment), § 4.2.1 and § 4.2.1.4 (effective Dec. 15, 2023; current per amendment check)

## Important catch-all limitation
The policy also says that **services other than those listed in Section 3.2 are not covered**. Section 3.2 includes the covered ambulance service criteria, including emergency services as defined there.  
[Ambulance Services](https://medicaid.ncdhhs.gov/15-ambulance-services/download?attachment), § 4.2.1.4; see also § 3.2 (effective Dec. 15, 2023; current per amendment check)

If you want, I can also turn this into a shorter **client-friendly checklist** or explain when NC Medicaid **will** cover ambulance transport.
